{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "userdb-lev-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.82: `userdb-lev` -- a LEV program, as MOVES 5 runs one. THC, CO, NOx, NMHC and the PM2.5 group (total, EC, sulfate, NonECPM, aerosol water) at running and start exhaust for the passenger car (21), passenger truck (31) and light commercial truck (32), every fuel MOVES adds, in Washtenaw County, DEFAULT domain, 2020, August, weekday, hour 7, from the default database plus a USER INPUT DATABASE (`<databaseselections>`) built EXACTLY as MOVES 5's LEV tool builds it (`inputs/washtenaw-userdb-lev.esm`: MOVES5_MyLEVS_Template.sql keeping model-year groups 1999-2003 and 2010-2017) -- one table, emissionRateByAge, 48,657 rows of the default's emissionRateByAgeLEV.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is the row merge (`erba_mergedMeanBaseRate`): MasterLoop merges the user database before the default database with INSERT IGNORE, so the LEV rows replace the default rates at their keys. The cohorts 1999-2003 and 2010-2017 of gasoline, diesel and E85 at regulatory classes 20 and 30 read LEV rates; 1980-1998, 2004-2009 and 2018-2020 read default rates, among them 1994-1998 and 2004-2009, which the LEV table covers and the user did not keep; 2017 reads LEV rates only where the LEV table has a row (half of class 30, none of class 20). NMHC is chained from LEV-rated THC, so it moves with it; the PM2.5 group does not move: the LEV table's EC and NonECPM rows are all at model-year group 45 (2025), so none is kept here and the PM2.5 group of a 2020 run reads default rates (`userdb-lev-2025` reads them). Execution database emissionRateByAge: 1,384,677 rows at the run's pollutant-processes, reproduced exactly by the merge in pandas, 48,657 of them the user's.\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to the chain's `rateSurvivorCount`; `n_sourceBin` 2 and `n_physicsRow` 7 from `sampleVehiclePopulation` and `sourceUseTypePhysics` for 21, 31 and 32.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "user-input-database",
      "lev"
    ]
  },
